.\" Manpage for bocl - BOCL Bootstrap Common Lisp.
.TH BOCL 1 "2026-06-25" "bocl 1.3.4" "BOCL Common Lisp"
.SH NAME
bocl \- BOCL Bootstrap Common Lisp interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bocl
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bocl
is a Common Lisp implementation built from a small C kernel plus a
runtime-loaded Lisp prelude.  Run without a script it enters an interactive
read\-eval\-print loop; it can also load files and evaluate forms given on the
command line, then optionally drop into the REPL.
.PP
On start\-up
.B bocl
loads its system Lisp files (the prelude and supporting files); see
.B FILES
and
.BR ENVIRONMENT .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print
.RB ( LISP\-IMPLEMENTATION\-VERSION )
and exit.
.TP
.BI \-E " encoding"
Set the character encodings.
.TP
.BI \-Eterminal " encoding\fR, \fB\-\-terminal\-encoding " encoding
Character encoding for
.BR *TERMINAL\-IO* .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-norc ", " \-\-no\-init
Suppress loading the default init file
.IR ~/.boclrc .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prelude
Suppress loading the prelude (bare kernel only).
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-q ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-\-silent
With
.BR \-\-batch ,
also suppress heralds and prompts.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-batch
Exit on end of file on
.BR *STANDARD\-INPUT* .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Raise verbosity (banner,
.BR *LOAD\-VERBOSE* ,
.BR *COMPILE\-VERBOSE* ).
.TP
.B \-\-print
Set
.B *LOAD\-PRINT*
and
.BR *COMPILE\-PRINT* .
.TP
.B \-\-dump
Dump the heap.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sigtrap
Do not trap signals (for running under a debugger).
.TP
.BI \-\-on\-error " action"
What to do when an
.B unhandled
error reaches the top level
.RB ( \-on\-error
is a legacy alias).
.I action
is one of:
.RS
.TP
.B exit
Report the condition and exit the process (status 1).  The default.
.TP
.B debug
Enter the interactive debugger
.RB ( INVOKE\-DEBUGGER ):
condition, backtrace, restart menu, debug REPL.
.TP
.B abort
Report and return to the top\-level REPL (no debugger; process stays alive).
.TP
.B appease
Like
.BR abort ,
but while loading a file a failing top\-level form is reported and skipped so the
load continues to the end.
.RE
.IP
Published to Lisp as
.BR BOCL:*ON\-ERROR* .
.TP
.BI \-i " file\fR, \fB\-\-init " file
Load
.I file
as an init file (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-x " form\fR, \fB\-e " form\fR, \fB\-\-eval " form
Evaluate
.I form
(quote it for the shell).
.TP
.BI \-l " file\fR, \fB\-\-load " file
Load
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-p " package\fR, \fB\-\-package " package
Start in
.IR package .
.TP
.BR \-repl ", " \-\-repl
Enter the REPL when argument processing is done (default).
.TP
.BR \-quit ", " \-\-quit
Quit when argument processing is done.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait
Wait for a keypress after termination.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOCL_PRELUDE
If set to a readable path, used as the prelude instead of the search below.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/libexec/bocl/prelude.lisp
The installed prelude and the other system Lisp files
.RI ( cl\-exports.lisp ", " bignum.lisp ", " bignum\-integration.lisp )
loaded at start\-up.  The default
.I PREFIX
is
.IR /opt/local .
.TP
.I ~/.boclrc
Per\-user init file, loaded unless
.B \-\-no\-init
is given.
.PP
At start\-up the prelude is located by, in order:
.B $BOCL_PRELUDE;
paths relative to the executable
.RI ( ../libexec/bocl/ ", " ../bootstrap/ ", " ../share/bocl/ );
then standard install paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
The user manual
.RI ( PREFIX/share/doc/bocl/documentation.pdf ),
the specifications
.RI ( PREFIX/share/doc/bocl/specifications.pdf ),
and the debugger specification
.RI ( PREFIX/share/doc/bocl/debugger\-specifications.org ).
